From 08a74b8b13ec81dcf3c9b40200896429314d4a9c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 15:57:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] arrange: pretest of the deep children (count-only
 filters, opts.pretest_min)

From 5 vectors placed (the (2,3)/(3,2) children, ~85% of all nodes at
N >= 11k, nearly all dead at the count and forward checks after their two
filters), the filters first only count the entries they keep and or them
into the unions (FILTER_COUNT, no compress or store, a byte of keep mask
per 8 entries); the lists are compressed from the keep masks (PT_APPLY)
only for the children that pass those checks. The same children die, so
nodes and squares are unchanged (also checked per sampled r1).

r1-sampled, paired against fdb77fc: x1.107 / 1.120 / 1.026 / 1.170 at
N = 15.2k / 16.4k / 20.5k / 23k (geometric mean 1.105), x1.06 at
N = 7.6-8.9k, x1.01 at 2.5k; bench/prod.txt -2.6%, full.txt -0.8%,
quick.txt +1.3%.

--pretest-min K in bench and msearch (0 = off); fuzz_arrange variants with
the pretest from 1, 3, 4 vectors placed, each also checked to visit the
same nodes as with the pretest off. Not kept, with numbers in
research/ideas.md: a lower threshold for the diagonal-first V_d searches
(4: x1.05-1.06, below the 1.08 bar) and the gated extra cross/support
round at the surviving (2,2) children (x1.01-1.04).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01GSaYLGdzq6d82nBLeSZFgB
